# The Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) arm64 packages the Linux client's arm64 .deb and
# .rpm are compiled and linked against: the development packages of what it
# links (FreeType, HarfBuzz, fontconfig, GLib and GIO, libsecret, PipeWire),
# the headers SDL3 builds its backends from (Wayland, X11, xkbcommon, ALSA,
# D-Bus, libdecor, EGL and GL), glibc's, and every library those depend on,
# which the linker reads to resolve them. Unpacked by sysroot_ubuntu_arm64.sh
# into third_party/sysroot-ubuntu-24.04-arm64/.
#
# Each line: package, version, sha256 of the .deb, its path under
# https://ports.ubuntu.com/ubuntu-ports/. The versions are noble's release
# pocket, which the archive never removes, so a pin here never stops resolving;
# glibc is 2.39, the client's floor (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, ARCH-20). The list
# was read from the release pocket's signed index (dists/noble/InRelease) for
# main and universe, following each package's Depends and Pre-Depends and
# leaving out programs, documentation and daemons, which a link never reads.
